translate en b01_001:
    "Malang, five in the afternoon. The sky was dark as night. Kai, seventeen, was on his way home from school — and the rain started pouring before he could make it back."

translate en b01_002:
    kai_hati "Ugh. Of course it starts now. Didn't even bring a plastic cover for my bag. All my books are gonna get soaked."

translate en b01_003:
    "He ran. Not toward the main road — there was nothing out there but car horns and ankle-deep puddles. He ducked into a narrow gap between two buildings, deeper and deeper... until his feet stopped on their own."

translate en b01_004:
    kai_hati "...What alley is this? I swear I've never come through here before."

translate en b01_005:
    "A dead-end alley. Always damp, like the rain here never quite finished falling. And at the very end, half hidden behind a dark wall, stood a small shop with a crooked wooden sign."

translate en b01_006:
    kai_hati "\"Gema Masa.\" A cassette shop? Seriously, cassette shops still exist?"

translate en b01_007:
    "He pushed the door open. A little bell chimed. Strangely, the second he stepped inside, the rain sounded miles away — like he'd left it at the door."

translate en b01_008:
    kai_hati "Warm in here. Smells like old paper... and jasmine tea. Tall shelves packed wall-to-wall with cassettes. Is this a shop or a museum?"

translate en b01_009:
    ageng "Weather's not being very friendly out there, huh?"

translate en b01_010:
    "Kai jumped. Behind the counter, an elderly man rose from a rocking chair. His hair was white, combed neatly back. He looked to be in his sixties, maybe, yet the way he stood was completely unhurried."

translate en b01_011:
    kai "Uh— yeah, Pak. Sorry... I just ducked in to wait out the rain for a bit. Um— I'm dripping all over your floor. Really sorry, Pak."

translate en b01_012:
    ageng "Take it easy. This shop's floor is used to rainwater. Monggo, have a seat. Dry yourself off."

translate en b01_013:
    "Without asking his name or what he wanted, Pak Ageng poured tea from an old teapot into a small ceramic cup and slid it over. Next to the cup sat a little plate of traditional market snacks."

translate en b01_014:
    kai "Oh— you really didn't have to, Pak... {i}(sits down, cupping his hands around the cup){/i} ...Thanks, Pak."

translate en b01_015:
    ageng "Drink up. You're shivering."

translate en b01_016:
    kai "{i}(takes a sip){/i} ...Mmm, that's good. Just the right amount of sweet. {i}(pauses, looking at the shelves){/i} Pak, are these all cassettes? I mean... do people still buy cassette tapes nowadays?"

translate en b01_017:
    ageng "They do. Some people come here looking for old music. {i}(walks over to the shelves, trailing his fingers along the tape spines){/i} But some come not to hear yesterday, kid. They come to hear tomorrow."

translate en b01_018:
    kai "...Tomorrow?"

translate en b01_019:
    ageng "Tomorrow."

translate en b01_020:
    "Kai's heart skipped a beat. The cup in his hands nearly tipped over."

translate en b01_021:
    kai_hati "Hear... tomorrow? Did he just say hear tomorrow?"

translate en b01_022:
    kai "Wait, you mean... the tapes can— they have tomorrow's sounds on them? For real?"

translate en b01_023:
    ageng "{i}(pulls a Regular Cassette from the shelf and sets it gently on the counter){/i} Recorded on this tape is sound from your tomorrow. Conversations that haven't happened yet. Sixty seconds. Just tomorrow's sound."

translate en b01_024:
    kai "{i}(swallows hard){/i} Sixty seconds..."

translate en b01_025:
    ageng "And one rule. This is the most important one, so listen closely. {i}(looks straight at Kai){/i} Don't try to change it. Ojo. If you force it to change, the tape gets tangled."

translate en b01_026:
    "Pak Ageng laid three Regular Cassettes side by side. All three held tomorrow's sounds — only the covers were different: one showed rain on a tin roof, one showed a bustling market, and one showed an alley in the morning."

translate en b01_027:
    ageng "Pick one. Whichever you like. Usually people go with the first one that catches their eye."

translate en b01_028a:
    ageng "Hmm. A kid who likes the sound of rain. {i}(smiles faintly){/i} Usually folks like that have noisy minds."

translate en b01_028b:
    ageng "The market. Loud, but honest. At the market, none of the sounds are faked."

translate en b01_028c:
    ageng "A quiet alley in the morning. You like places nobody else has touched yet, huh."

translate en b01_029:
    "Kai held the cassette he chose. The plastic felt rough, the tape inside taut and intact. It was light — yet somehow his hands were shaking."

translate en b02_001:
    "Pak Ageng settled back into his rocking chair. The wood creaked in a slow, steady rhythm that almost made Kai sleepy — except his head was only getting louder."

translate en b02_002:
    ageng "This world runs along its own line, kid. Humans always feel like they're holding the wheel. When really... we're just scared passengers."

translate en b02_003:
    kai "Pak... I still can't wrap my head around this. How can tomorrow's sound already be here right now?"

translate en b02_004:
    ageng "{i}(doesn't answer; slides over a plate of klepon){/i} Eat first. With klepon, you pop the whole thing in at once — don't bite it in half, or it'll squirt everywhere."

translate en b02_005:
    kai "{i}(picks one up and pops it in whole){/i} —Mmh! {i}(startled as melted palm sugar bursts in his mouth){/i} ...Whoa, super sweet. That's really good, Pak."

translate en b02_006:
    ageng "See? That's real enough, right? {i}(smiles){/i} Now listen. In this shop, there are two kinds of cassettes."

translate en b02_007:
    ageng "First, the one you're holding. A Regular Cassette. C-60, Type I. Cheap — just a few bills from your allowance. Sixty seconds of tomorrow's sound. Only tomorrow. The effect is mild: after you listen, you might feel relieved... or you might just get even more anxious."

translate en b02_008:
    kai "And... what about those, Pak? {i}(points to a special shelf holding just a handful of blood-red cassettes){/i}"

translate en b02_009:
    ageng "{i}(his voice turns noticeably colder){/i} Those are Red Cassettes. C-90, Type IV, Metal. Stronger. Still sixty seconds — but from much further out. Six months to a year ahead."

translate en b02_010:
    kai_hati "A year...? I could find out if I graduate or not. I could find out if my life still feels this suffocating a year from now."

translate en b02_011:
    kai "How much are they, Pak?"

translate en b02_012:
    ageng "Not money."

translate en b02_013:
    kai "Then what?"

translate en b02_014:
    ageng "The happiest memory you currently have. You trade it. That memory disappears from your head — permanently. Pulled straight into the tape to fuel it. A trip that far takes a lot of energy, kid. And there's no purer energy than a person's happiness."

translate en b02_015:
    "The teacup in Kai's hand suddenly felt ice-cold."

translate en b02_016:
    ageng "More often than not, the future people hear isn't worth the memory they threw away. They regret it later — once they realize they don't have a reason left to smile when they think back on the past."

translate en b02_017:
    kai_hati "My happiest memory... I don't even have that many. If even one of them vanished... {i}(long pause){/i} No. Not yet. I'm not that desperate."

translate en b02_018:
    kai "I'll... just take the regular one, Pak."

translate en b02_019:
    "Kai dug into his jacket pocket. His bills were slightly damp from the rain."

translate en b02_020a:
    kai "Here you go, Pak. Exact change, right?"

translate en b02_021a:
    ageng "Spot on. {i}(takes a tiny blank cassette from under the counter and slips it into the paper bag with Kai's tape){/i} Here's a little bonus. A mini blank cassette. Hang on to it. Who knows — maybe one day you'll need to record something that's truly yours."

translate en b02_020b:
    kai "Pak... any chance of a small discount? My allowance for this week is down to—"

translate en b02_021b:
    ageng "{i}(shakes his head gently, not angry){/i} Prices in this shop aren't up for bargaining, kid. Not because I'm stingy. Because what you're buying isn't the plastic."

translate en b02_022b:
    kai "...Right, Pak. Sorry. Here, full price."

translate en b02_020c:
    kai "Pak, could I... pay in installments? Half now, and the rest next Friday—"

translate en b02_021c:
    ageng "{i}(chuckles softly){/i} You can't pay for tomorrow in installments, kid. It shows up all at once, whether you're ready or not."

translate en b02_022c:
    kai "{i}(sighs and pulls out the money){/i} ...Fair point. Here, Pak."

translate en b02_023:
    ageng "{i}(slides the cassette into a clear case and hands it over){/i} This one's for Friday. Sixty seconds."

translate en b02_024:
    kai "{i}(reads the handwritten label on the tape){/i} ...Friday."

translate en b02_025:
    ageng "One more thing, before you head home. These tapes never lie. But human ears mishear things all the time. Remember that."

translate en b02_026a:
    "At the mouth of the alley, an orange cat sat sheltering beneath a flower pot, staring at Kai like they were old friends. Kai crouched down for a moment."

translate en b02_027a:
    kai "You live around here? ...Keep an eye on the shop, okay?"

translate en b02_026b:
    "The street was still wet and busy. On a bulletin board near the intersection, a school showcase poster hung half-torn. Kai glanced at it in passing, then kept walking — the cassette in his bag feeling heavier than all his textbooks combined."

translate en b02_028:
    kai_hati "I've got Friday's sound sitting in my bag. I should be excited. Why do I feel... oh well. I'll just listen to it tonight."

translate en b03_001:
    "Kai's bedroom was cramped and full of old stuff: stacks of comics, posters peeling at the corners, and on his desk — his beat-up silver Walkman. The paint on the edges had chipped off long ago, but the buttons still had a solid click to them. Click."

translate en b03_002:
    kai_hati "Okay. Okay. Just sixty seconds. If it's total nonsense, then some eccentric old guy just played a prank on me. And if it's real... {i}(takes a breath){/i} ...I'll worry about that later."

translate en b03_003:
    "Tape in. Bulky headphones with cracked ear pads over his ears. Kai shut his eyes. Then — play."

translate en b03_004:
    kai "{i}(yanks the headphones off, breathing fast){/i} ...Hah. Hahaha. No. No way. I do have Bu Sarah's class tomorrow, my brain's just... just making stuff up. I'm overthinking it, that's all. {i}(pauses, staring at the Walkman){/i} ...Right?"

translate en b03_005:
    "Bu Sarah walked in carrying a stack of books and slammed them onto the desk. Just like on the tape. Determined to prove the cassette wrong, Kai copied down every single number, stared at the whiteboard until his eyes stung, and didn't look away once."

translate en b03_006:
    kai_hati "Focus. Focus. Today I'm the most diligent student in all of Malang. Zero reason for her to—"

translate en b03_007:
    "His pen ran out of ink. On reflex, he rummaged through his metal pencil case. Clatter, clank. In the dead-silent classroom, it echoed ridiculously loud. Bu Sarah stopped writing. Turned around. Slowly."

translate en b03_008:
    kai_hati "...Don't. Don't say that line. Don't—"

translate en b03_009:
    bu_sarah "Kai! Have you really not been paying attention to me this whole time?!"

translate en b03_010:
    "The whole class turned to look. Kai's face burned all the way to his ears."

translate en b03_011:
    bu_sarah "Get out of my class right now. Do the exercises on pages fifty through sixty in the library. Don't come back until my period is over!"

translate en b03_012:
    kai "{i}(stands up on shaky legs, silently packing his books){/i} ...Yes, Bu."

translate en b03_013:
    "Out in the hallway, Kai leaned back against the cold concrete wall. His hands were still trembling."

translate en b03_014:
    kai_hati "Word for word. Exactly the same. Her angry tone, the pauses, everything. That wasn't suggestion. That was... a recording. An actual recording of today, that I listened to yesterday. {i}(stares at the blank cassette in his pocket){/i} If something as small as getting yelled at by a teacher is that accurate... what else is sitting on the shelves in that shop?"

translate en b03_015:
    kai_hati "I should feel calm now. I've got a way to peek at tomorrow. {i}(pause){/i} So why does it feel like someone's squeezing my throat?"

translate en b04_001:
    "From that day on, the ever-wet alley became Kai's mandatory detour after school. Gema Masa turned into something like a pharmacy. And those cassettes — a heavy-duty tranquilizer for his anxiety."

translate en b04_002:
    ageng "The usual?"

translate en b04_003:
    kai "The usual, Pak. {i}(hands over the allowance money he'd set aside){/i} What snack do you have today, Pak?"

translate en b04_004:
    ageng "Putu. Eat first before you head home. You're way too skinny, kid."

translate en b04_005:
    "At night, the same ritual: dark room, headphones, sixty seconds of tomorrow's sound. And strangely — at first, the tapes actually helped."

translate en b04_006:
    kai_hati "Splashing water... an angkot... Don't walk along the main-road sidewalk tomorrow morning. Leave earlier, take the inner side."

translate en b04_007:
    "The next day, from a safe distance, Kai watched an angkot plow straight through a puddle just like on the tape — while his uniform stayed spotless. He cracked a small smile to himself."

translate en b04_008:
    kai_hati "...It works. You actually can outsmart it."

translate en b04_009:
    ibu_kaset "Where are my motorbike keys? I could've sworn I left them right here yesterday..."

translate en b04_010:
    "The next morning, before Mom woke up, Kai set the motorbike keys on the dining table. Quietly. Like a secret agent."

translate en b04_011:
    kai_hati "For the first time... I woke up without my chest feeling tight. I know what's coming. I can prepare. {i}(smiles){/i} This is it. This is what I've been looking for all along."

translate en b04_012:
    kai_kaset "My hand... it's bleeding."

translate en b04_013:
    kai "{i}(shuts off the Walkman, pale){/i} No. Not this time. {i}(gets up and starts clearing every glass object out of his room){/i} Picture frame — out. Drinking glass — out. Small mirror — out. Tomorrow I'm not leaving my room. Period. Not even going out for dinner. It's not gonna happen. No way."

translate en b04_014:
    "All day long, Kai locked himself inside. No broken glass. No blood. The clock hit nighttime — the danger window had passed. Immensely relieved, he stood up to turn off the light."

translate en b04_015:
    kai_hati "I won. I beat the tape—"

translate en b04_016:
    "His foot caught the curled edge of the rug. He lost his balance. His hand shot out for the desk — and his elbow knocked over the one piece of glass he'd missed: a photo frame on his study desk."

translate en b04_017:
    kai "Agh! {i}(falls, his palm landing on the shards){/i} ...My hand... it's bleeding."

translate en b04_018:
    "Exact match. Even the intonation was identical. Wincing, Kai stared at the blood pooling in his palm — and understood something terrifying: trying to dodge it was the exact thing that led him straight into it."

translate en b04_019:
    kai_hati "The tape... it tangled. {i}(long pause){/i} Pak Ageng said... if you try to change it, the tape gets tangled. {i}(stares at his hastily bandaged hand){/i} ...And yet I haven't learned my lesson. That's the scariest part. I'm not even deterred. Tomorrow I'm still going back to that shop. I still need to know what tomorrow holds."

translate en b04_020:
    ageng "{i}(notices the bandage on Kai's hand, then holds his gaze for a long moment){/i} ...You tried to change it, didn't you."

translate en b04_021:
    kai "{i}(looks down){/i} ...Yeah, Pak."

translate en b04_022:
    ageng "And?"

translate en b04_023:
    kai "The tape got tangled. {i}(pause){/i} But I still came back, Pak. I still... need it."

translate en b04_024:
    "Pak Ageng didn't scold him. He just took a Regular Cassette and set it on the counter, same as always. Only this time, he didn't immediately turn away."

translate en b04_025a:
    ageng "{i}(slides the cassette slowly toward Kai){/i} Hmm. {i}(says nothing more; the wall clock in the shop ticks louder than usual){/i}"

translate en b04_025b:
    ageng "{i}(gives a small nod){/i} Smart kid. With medicine, you know... it's usually not the medicine itself that makes it poison. It's the dose."

translate en b04_025c:
    ageng "{i}(smiles faintly){/i} Then don't take this one either. Go home. Go to sleep without knowing if it'll rain tomorrow — like everybody else."

translate en b04_026c:
    kai "{i}(stares at the cassette for a long time... then slowly shakes his head){/i} ...I can't yet, Pak. Sorry. {i}(picks up the cassette){/i} Maybe I'll quit tomorrow. Or the day after."

translate en b04_027:
    "Whatever Kai said that afternoon, his feet still carried him home with a cassette in his bag. The only thing that changed was how tightly he held on to it."
